WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.680
Hey, everyone.

2
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.440
My name is Sahil and I'm one of the engineers here at Tessl.

3
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.040
I'm going to be in New York and in Boston on the 16th and 17th of September,

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.280
talking about how we've built our software factory here at Tessl

5
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.840
and what engineering looks like in an AI native world.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.840
I'm going to be diving into the components that we've built out,

7
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.240
why they're there, why they're useful, the mistakes that we've made along the way,

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.000
the sort of metrics that we focused on early that actually didn't end up helping

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.240
us, and the ones that actually did, and all the different quirks and features

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.280
that ended up building out the factory that we have today.

11
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.040
This is going to be a much more practical look into the factory that we have here

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.600
at Tessl and some of the specifics on how it works

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.360
and why we made some of the decisions that we did.

14
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.120
Go to tessl.io/events and I hope to see you all there.
